; ---- what the fighting sounds like ----------------------------------------
;
; Every name here is a moment the client raises, named after the creature or the
; shot it happened to, and falling back a word at a time where nothing is named:
; died.Warden.normal finds died.Warden, then died. So a creature added later is
; never silent, and one given its own line is heard as itself.
;
;   fired.<Template>      a blow or a shot of its weapon (Dungeon.namedFor names
;                         every weapon after its holder); fired for a shot of a
;                         skill, which has no weapon
;   cast.<Hero>.<Key>     a skill of his went off (Dungeon, on the CastSkill order)
;   hurt.<Template>       its health went down: the blow landing, and its pain
;   spawned.<Template>    it came into sight: a growl, a roar, a battle cry
;   died.<Template>       it died
;   struck.<Projectile>   a shot vanished on somebody: it landed
;   step.<surface>        his foot on the picture painted under him (Soundscape);
;                         step for the descent's stone and anything unnamed
;
; Who recorded what is in CREDITS.md: rubberduck's three CC0 packs, Vehicle's
; weapons and apparel, artisticdude's RPG pack, HaelDB's grunts and yells,
; Fantozzi's footsteps and Kenney's, all CC0. Each was trimmed, levelled to the
; same peak and made mono, since OpenAL will not place a stereo sound.

; ---- blows and shots ------------------------------------------------------

; A shot of a skill, which no weapon fired: the wave, the volley, the nova.
Sound
  Name = fired
  Channel = Effects
  Positional = Yes
  Gain = 0.45
  Files = [audio/sfx/weapon/swing_1.ogg, audio/sfx/weapon/swing_2.ogg, audio/sfx/weapon/swing_3.ogg]
End

